  "prompt_used": "Review everything we discussed in this chat and all the research you gathered, then brainstorm how to turn those ideas into practical improvements for Coqui before writing code. If you discover gaps, conflicting findings, outdated assumptions, or unanswered implementation questions, conduct additional targeted research using primary papers and current official documentation before settling on a design. Consider profit-taking rules based on portfolio gains, percentage growth, or dollar milestones, with safeguards that distinguish investment profits from deposits, avoid repeatedly withdrawing the same gains, and preserve enough operating capital for future trades. Treat winning-trade counts as optional triggers rather than proof of profitability, and distinguish selling into cash from withdrawing money to the user. Design around realistic small starting balances, accounting for fees, spreads, slippage, fractional orders, minimum trade sizes, concentration, turnover, and the trade-off between compounding and withdrawals. Evaluate the researched strategies—including trend following with cash, buffered momentum rotation, breakout, bounded mean reversion, strategy blends, cost-aware execution, and calibrated ML filters—and identify which existing capabilities we can reuse, simplify, or improve. Challenge each idea, explain its failure modes, and prioritize evidence over complexity or promised returns. Preserve previous negative research findings and existing safety controls. After brainstorming and resolving necessary research questions, produce a concrete, phased implementation plan covering the architecture, data and accounting requirements, strategy changes, settings and user experience, dependencies, tests, and acceptance criteria. Separate promising hypotheses from validated behavior, define how we will evaluate strategies across small portfolio sizes using realistic costs and fresh evidence, and sequence the work into manageable steps that can then be implemented in the app without prematurely enabling live trading or automatic withdrawals.",
